Overview

We are looking for a Configuration Tools SW Engineer to join a global engineering team developing software tools that simplify the configuration of embedded systems used in modern automotive platforms.

As the automotive industry continues to evolve through electrification, connectivity, autonomous driving, and software-defined vehicle architectures, you will contribute to innovative solutions that enable the next generation of automotive technologies.

You will be part of an international team working on a diverse portfolio of tools, ranging from embedded C-based solutions to advanced applications integrated with modeling environments. Collaborating in a SAFe (Scaled Agile Framework) environment, you will participate in the design, development, and enhancement of configuration tools that deliver reliable, intuitive, and high-performance software solutions for customers worldwide.

Responsibilities

Design, develop, maintain, and enhance large-scale software applications for configuration tools;
Contribute to the implementation of new features and improvements for existing software products;
Develop customer-specific solutions to address complex technical requirements;
Collaborate with globally distributed engineering teams throughout the software development lifecycle;
Participate in software architecture discussions, technical design, implementation, testing, and code reviews;
Apply object-oriented programming principles and embedded software expertise to develop reliable and maintainable solutions;
Create and maintain scripts to automate development, testing, and configuration activities;
Support the continuous improvement of software development processes and Agile practices;
Work closely with internal stakeholders to understand requirements and translate them into technical solutions;
Ensure software quality, performance, maintainability, and compliance with established development standards;
Stay up to date with emerging technologies and contribute to innovation initiatives, including AI-assisted development where applicable.

Requirements

Strong object-oriented programming experience in at least one of the following languages: Java, C++, C#;
Solid experience with embedded software development using C;
Good understanding of embedded systems concepts and software architecture;
Basic knowledge of Artificial Intelligence concepts;
Proficiency in at least one scripting language (Python, Bash, PowerShell, or similar);
Experience working on medium to large-scale software development projects;
Strong collaboration and teamwork skills in an international environment;
Good understanding of software development processes and Agile methodologies;
Professional proficiency in spoken and written English;
Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Electronics, or a related technical field.

Nice to have

Experience with Eclipse plug-in development;
Previous technical leadership or mentoring experience;
Knowledge of software quality standards, particularly in embedded software development;
Experience participating in software quality audits;
Strong presentation and communication skills;
Experience with MATLAB/Simulink;
Familiarity with the automotive industry and embedded software toolchains.

What We Offer

Opportunity to work on complex international embedded software projects;
Exposure to software release validation, quality engineering and automation;
Technical training and guidance from senior engineers;
A collaborative engineering environment with knowledge-sharing initiatives;
Meal vouchers as part of your monthly benefits;
Private medical insurance;
25 days of annual paid leave under a full-time employment contract;
Flexible working arrangements, aligned with project requirements;
Access to technical training programs and professional development resources.

Ready to embed yourself in the future? Let’s partner with us to power what’s next!

